{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_067578336e57aff5da169d9072c7647040d46ad411072e438f50e541efb240a8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"guanyilun/agent-sh@8038ae7730eb snapshot a723232a0e326851","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0c2ef859f0f39b833e277810b7c1b54ccad74187ac140ed450175785a0c6d7c4","slc_9f4f0de3bf3d4c99db508c9402773c8a8ca8b67671508b952d387f052f899973"],"source_ids":["src_f31d81881f61550b9f2cc60fb4886bf0"],"text":"Core tools include bash, read_file, write_file, edit_file, grep (via ripgrep), glob, ls, and list_skills; conversation_recall is registered by the rolling-history extension rather than being a core tool.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0f3235d2e61cb0fcd90c541c743035609fc5f0683eb1477a21907406edde1be6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"guanyilun/agent-sh@8038ae7730eb snapshot a723232a0e326851","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_782a7aa67790bedeec0781547e6248f13b6cfdb4eb628d191fd787bc53b37945","slc_b3f00d97d457eacd6e94ea0c14cb138a375ae2e5c3e645969810fb3d7d36059f","slc_bd1b89bee317238506de2004e3459b985a8e7b9cd5184c7b81063c9b61cf4405","slc_e06ef58dc0587994cfdb28a11f1151b443d6ac8b7f896cf3a9d8ede77fc83937"],"source_ids":["src_f31d81881f61550b9f2cc60fb4886bf0"],"text":"Conversation state is an OpenAI-compatible messages array; ash auto-compacts when estimated prompt tokens cross autoCompactThreshold (default 0.5) of the model's context window, and older turns are evicted to a persistent rolling-history store browsable via conversation_recall.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_24353849ad0ed947a8ad3f4840c791e69c33d4cc228fc4d3dae90461387469b5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"guanyilun/agent-sh@8038ae7730eb snapshot a723232a0e326851","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_796070bc205e299f00197f67e6db572f60ea6119428c67a975264911f1d32886","slc_86748de6bcc4364920c4e03681f9df0994f0c0f57f2b02a70906dabac8495e13","slc_e5753a45aa1d19ba9ec09a7c5623b3549255a09fb384492634edbb0f8389ee72"],"source_ids":["src_f31d81881f61550b9f2cc60fb4886bf0"],"text":"Tools implement a `ToolDefinition` interface with name, description, JSON Schema input_schema, an execute function with optional streaming onChunk callback, and flags like modifiesFiles, readOnly, and showOutput.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_255fef59932579011fbb349995b5c32192b222fe37186815f0789074119438aa","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"guanyilun/agent-sh@8038ae7730eb snapshot a723232a0e326851","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_20165ca98635b28ac5c9c9b2d1f1c84f6150867d6125f0682830d35d0f52fbe3","slc_42f6254fc6f072fb4e5d6adf2f35077ed0e599c85d548bcc7fa1cb9aa1628977","slc_43b7714b75463ef2d331400bec48a725da14189851eb209f576fad8091db9ae0"],"source_ids":["src_f31d81881f61550b9f2cc60fb4886bf0"],"text":"The agent runs a tool loop with no hard iteration limit; side-effect-free tools run in parallel via Promise.all while side-effecting tools run sequentially, and results over maxResultBytes (default 100KB) are head+tail truncated.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_308942903fd7f609a53ce97e769f5c6d0f4e5f9994ea5876403db915cd756216","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"guanyilun/agent-sh@8038ae7730eb snapshot a723232a0e326851","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0c2ef859f0f39b833e277810b7c1b54ccad74187ac140ed450175785a0c6d7c4","slc_2739692662c45c93bbd90e310fb2713c4cceb5cc9d6398b888a6640148292db2","slc_a076f31e6259b875d19c2313282535ae654369ca36bf3cc707d07168587e689e"],"source_ids":["src_872821a22f605331bc831be51c1c70db","src_f31d81881f61550b9f2cc60fb4886bf0"],"text":"The bundled frontend is a shell on top of node-pty, and the grep tool searches file contents via ripgrep; ash works with any OpenAI-compatible API including built-in providers openrouter, openai, deepseek, ollama, zai-coding-plan, and opencode.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3b0a98f1549298b6ec64e89cb797ebfcfa19117dca8e14c2482e1a2ee22f2fe4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"guanyilun/agent-sh@8038ae7730eb snapshot a723232a0e326851","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_21fc9cd4100c41b64184e1b6a8c315a3ca2415b6918447041074339adcac6190"],"source_ids":["src_f31d81881f61550b9f2cc60fb4886bf0"],"text":"By default every tool runs without gating ('yolo mode'); the kernel has no permission opinion, and gating extensions can interpose confirmation or policy checks via tool advisors.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5153fe7e95e306e1ea78fea87d7fdc04b96c6cb12bf9b20409fccd6c616e5f20","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=skills-patterns","setting":"guanyilun/agent-sh@8038ae7730eb snapshot a723232a0e326851","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3e72843d1e6ec7da6fa9a6a2629d64a62f1e29190fa96c385374daf0c3c7e019","slc_4e43af6fd4f78571fc1cfba9f89d89bec26afce6fc6e7fb04afc52b9495438b4","slc_7b2e70209c962da00275a617ebc069c51f2e50622de1b37bf208e3acbbe51c5d","slc_db335e3d7fbb4a5c1e8874191f1f6245741eae3011dfcc5ced294c0fdc52f3b2"],"source_ids":["src_f31d81881f61550b9f2cc60fb4886bf0"],"text":"Skills follow the Agent Skills standard: directories with a SKILL.md containing YAML frontmatter (required name and description); only metadata enters the system prompt, and the agent loads full content via read_file when needed.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5792c66312ba36d97aaf6feb35e6458f98eac19d66c140ce8970b00519f94949","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"guanyilun/agent-sh@8038ae7730eb snapshot a723232a0e326851","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0b4105d9bd1fd64d0973021cfd6734dfd0573ef515d78be641b9ecc5bf7753af"],"source_ids":["src_f31d81881f61550b9f2cc60fb4886bf0"],"text":"The default backend `ash` resolves providers, configures an LlmClient, calls any OpenAI-compatible API directly, and executes tools in a loop until the LLM finishes; it only activates once an apiKey and model are resolved.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_72ec5a38ad78b754541f1918afeae0ce3353e1c2f73dae817cca9e70248b941b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"guanyilun/agent-sh@8038ae7730eb snapshot a723232a0e326851","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8ad947087a66d3fda15227f98fac1a18a5285c874c525cc2ef33bb262378af60","slc_ca81535470dd8a4ec9407c350484250088fc8d5170939f090f3bb3cad9bcb7e8"],"source_ids":["src_872821a22f605331bc831be51c1c70db"],"text":"agent-sh is published as an npm package (`agent-sh`) with a license badge, installable globally via `npm install -g agent-sh`.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_753604f7f83b0d94d5fdeff1e2a2572d13c6e276b53336223acda03ba53113b5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"guanyilun/agent-sh@8038ae7730eb snapshot a723232a0e326851","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_64ffb0263e5cc7ee4cd0ee1dd8f165a1fe8438b31d3e1fd39f2e5441250762fe","slc_eb6cc94d26a23193eba2f74c8a5f01d5ef3da76e1c3fd095257af3342833796d"],"source_ids":["src_ee863c2c0bed58b5a9cae73a397c8980"],"text":"The architecture is a pure kernel (`createCore()`) providing EventBus, HandlerRegistry, Compositor, multi-backend coordination, and a default cwd handler, with agent, shell, TUI, and providers all loaded as extensions.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_761f9deeee81908f0ec6f7fdf178d4bd8daedaa8f19c8e542e1eba3b9e5a6c66","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"guanyilun/agent-sh@8038ae7730eb snapshot a723232a0e326851","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_103d367cd2eb90ed874b6d32f4fc1698440dd46228c260f5b9165c965cb35992"],"source_ids":["src_872821a22f605331bc831be51c1c70db"],"text":"Native Windows (cmd.exe/PowerShell) is not supported as the host shell; the README recommends running inside WSL for the full interactive experience, while headless/library/ACP-bridge usage may work.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c797267ff84e977963f684ad537fbf8a3b9a0d6a495cfec039f3491ce57f49ef","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"guanyilun/agent-sh@8038ae7730eb snapshot a723232a0e326851","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7edf5aa09de0dffa0ff372c710cbe9cd195c3fb0399a8de77900956086f21028"],"source_ids":["src_872821a22f605331bc831be51c1c70db"],"text":"The runtime requires Node.js 18+ and supports bash, zsh, and fish as host shells; other shells such as nushell are not yet wired up.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428"}
